AG Grid 33 is a key major version which enables significant bundle size reduction via modularisation. It also fully commits to the new theming API as default, adds new features across the grid together with improvements in developer experience, accessibility and performance:

1. [Bundle Size Reduction via Modularisation](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/modules/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com)
2. [Context Menu Async Items](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/context-menu/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com#context-menu-example)
3. [Customisation of Default Column Header Content](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/column-headers/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com#inner-header-component)
4. [Theming API Improvements](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/theming/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com)
5. [Native Support for Vue 3 Composition API](#native-support-for-vue-3-composition-api)

Please note that AG Grid 33 has breaking changes from AG Grid 32.X. We're providing [Codemods](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/upgrading-to-ag-grid-33/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com#codemods) to help you upgrade by automating the migration process as much as possible.

Please review the [migration guide](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/upgrading-to-ag-grid-33/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com) when planning to update to this version.

## Bundle Size Reduction

AG Grid 33 modularises the grid which allows you to import only the modules you need for the features you're using. This enables a significant reduction in bundle size which will vary between 20-40% depending on the features you're using.

This significant improvement required changes in the way the grid is imported on a page, which are [covered in the migration guide](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/upgrading-to-ag-grid-33/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com#changes-to-modules).

We're providing a [module selector](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/modules/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com) to help you find the modules you need and generates the necessary import code. This way you can start using the new modules and benefit from the bundle size reduction and improved loading times for AG Grid.

See this [documented here](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/upgrading-to-ag-grid-33/?ref=blog.ag-grid.com#changes-to-modules) and illustrated below:


